## Project Structure

```text
src/
├── lib/
│   ├── components/      # Reusable UI components
│   ├── api/             # Business logic and API services
│   ├── types/           # TypeScript type definitions
│   ├── stores/          # State management, stores, and context
│   ├── tests/           # Unit and integration tests
│   └── utils/           # Utility functions, helpers, constants, enums
│       ├── helpers/            # Helper functions
│       ├── constants/          # JSON constant data
│       └── enums/              # Enumerations
├── routes/             # SvelteKit routes and pages
│   ├── (company)/       # Company/marketing pages (about, careers, terms, etc.)
│   ├── (protected)/    # Authenticated user areas (dashboard, profile, wallet)
│   ├── [...path]/      # Catch-all route for dynamic paths
│   ├── 404/            # Error page handling
│   ├── auth/           # Authentication flows (login, signup, recovery)
│   ├── tasks/          # Task management and viewing
│   └── verify-email/   # Email verification process
└── stories/           # Storybook component stories
    ├── assets/         # Storybook assets (images, icons, documentation)
    ├── bidding/        # Bidding system component stories
    ├── messages/       # Messaging and chat component stories
    └── task/           # Task-related component stories
```

## Naming Conventions

- Use camelCase for variable names
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use kebab-case for routes names
- Use snake_case for assets
- File Naming and Location:
  - Components: src/lib/components/ExampleComponent.svelte
  - Services: src/lib/services/example.service.ts
  - Utils: src/lib/utils/exampleUtil.ts
  - Types: src/lib/types/exampleTypes.d.ts
  - Tests: src/lib/tests/example.test.ts
  - Stores: src/lib/stores/example.store.ts

